method_text = """
STEP 4: Spatial mapping method text

Observed and model-predicted fertility-index values were mapped using the 64 georeferenced soil sampling locations. The best-performing regularized model predictions were selected for each index: Lasso for Overall_SFI, ElasticNet for MNI, ElasticNet for MiNI and Lasso for SFI_5core. Observed, predicted and residual values were converted to point feature classes in WGS 84 and projected to UTM Zone 44N. Continuous fertility-index surfaces were generated using inverse distance weighting interpolation at 30 m spatial resolution within the point-covered Hanumakonda study boundary. Relative fertility-management zones were produced from the predicted index surfaces using lower, middle and upper tertile thresholds derived from predicted values. These spatial products represent interpolated observed and model-predicted fertility-index surfaces, not satellite-covariate digital soil maps.
"""

